{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And the sense of <b>for in their anger they killed a man, and in their pleasure they uprooted an ox</b> is that they committed the violence in their anger — for they were wrathful against Shechem — and in their pleasure — for they desired it — not through the negligence of the slain and not through their sin. Onkelos said (Onkelos on Genesis 49:6) that the meaning of שור is like שור in שורק, from \"daughters tread upon the wall\" (Genesis 49:22), and he translated in it again \"סנאה\", from \"her eyes regard with enmity\" (Psalms 92:12), and the sense is that they uprooted a city surrounded by a wall — its children and its women — after killing its men, and \"עקרו\" would be from \"it shall be uprooted\" (Zephaniah 2:4). And others explained (Radak in the name of Riva) that שור, the great one among beasts, is an allusion to Hamor and Shechem his son, prince of the land, as in \"his firstborn ox, majesty is his\" (Deuteronomy 33:17), \"the cows of Bashan that are in the mountain of Samaria\" (Amos 4:1), and thus Scripture calls great rulers by rams and he-goats. But what is correct in my eyes is according to the plain sense of the verse: it says that in their anger they killed every man of their anger, and in their pleasure — after their wrath subsided with the killing of the men — they uprooted every ox, an allusion to their livestock and their property, everything that was in the house and everything that was in the field. And he mentioned this to say that in their plot his soul did not enter into any of these things, not even to uproot from them livestock and property and to plunder their spoil at all, and \"עקרו\" is from \"you shall hamstring their horses\" (Joshua 11:6) — but it is all one expression and one matter:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The citation of Psalms 92:12 here corresponds to the Hebrew verse numbering in the Masoretic text; the phrase quoted (\"her eyes regard with enmity\") follows the reading implicit in Ramban's argument."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:46:55.309100141Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}